  "text_md": "events\n\n## Mandela Commemoration Medal Parade\n\n##### By Cpl Ally Rakoma Photos by S Sgt Lebogang Tlhaole\n\nt has been a year since the passing of the founding President of a democratic South Africa, the first Commander-in- Chief of the SANDF and Nobel\n\n# IPeace Prize recipient, the late\n\nMr Nelson Mandela.\n\nIn line with our country’s activities to commemorate the first anniversary of *Tata* Ma ndela’s death, the SANDF held a Mandela Commemorative Medal Parade at Air Force Base Waterkloof in Pretoria last month.\n\nPresident Jacob Zuma, the President of South Africa and Commander-in-Chief of the SANDF, was the main functionary at the medal parade. He awarded gold medals to SANDF men and women for their role in taking care of our statesman during the period when he was ill, his funeral, the mourning period arrangements, the lying-in- state at the Union Buildings and leading the state funeral at Qunu.\n\nPresident Zuma expressed his gratitude and admiration to the SANDF for carrying out its duties towards its first Commander-in- Chief. President Zuma said: “I can say with pride that the planning, execution and precision with which the SA National Defence Force (SANDF) performed its duties left no one in doubt about the capability of\n\n*LEFT: President* *Jacob Zuma,* *the President of* *South Africa and* *Commander-* *in-Chief of* *the SANDF,* *addresses* *the parade* *accompanied* *by the Minister* *of Defence* *and Military* *Veterans, Ms* *Nosiviwe Mapisa-* *Nqakula, and* *Lt Gen Norman* *Yengeni, the* *Chief of Human* *Resources.*\n\n#### 2 0 1 5 V O L 2 2 N O 1•\n\nour armed forces.”*ABOVE: Fltr: Mr Siphiwe Dlamini, Head of Communication, Prof* *Edna van Harte, the Chairperson of the Defence Force Service* He also thanked the international*Commission, Adv George Bizos, Veteran Human Rights Lawyer and* community for standing by South*Madiba’s close friend, Justice Dikgang Moseneke, the Deputy Chief* Africa as the world mourned the*Justice of the Constitutional Court of South Africa,* former statesman’s death on 5*Dr Sam Gulube, Secretary for Defence, and Mr Kebby Maphatsoe,* December 2013. President Zuma said:*the Deputy Minister of Defence and Military Veterans, at the* “We remain grateful for this support*Mandela Commemoration Medal Parade.*\n\n#### S A S O L D I E R\n",
